You know, I mean, some are further apart than others,

00:49:45.100 --> 00:49:50.320
but like, I think it seems like they average like 8, 9, or 10 away from each other

00:49:50.320 --> 00:49:51.580
as like another Essential Game.

00:49:51.760 --> 00:49:53.820
And it always feels like they're so far away from each other.

00:49:53.940 --> 00:49:56.920
But I do also think the percentage will drop a bit

00:49:56.920 --> 00:50:00.860
because I do think that we have...

00:50:01.500 --> 00:50:04.520
Our standards have gotten a little higher the more we've played

00:50:04.520 --> 00:50:08.860
and like kind of gotten familiar with the kinds of things we can expect

00:50:08.860 --> 00:50:12.640
from the NES.

00:50:13.080 --> 00:50:17.600
So I think that that also might play into like us voting for fewer games.

00:50:17.600 --> 00:50:26.040
Plus, I do agree with Sean that like while as the life of the NES goes on,

00:50:27.000 --> 00:50:30.340
inevitably like there's going to be progress in making games,

00:50:30.500 --> 00:50:32.860
but also the system has 900 games.

00:50:32.980 --> 00:50:34.420
There's got to be a lot of shovelware on there.

00:50:34.700 --> 00:50:36.460
So maybe that'll lower it.

00:50:36.540 --> 00:50:39.040
But it is hard to say because even on the, you know,

00:50:39.120 --> 00:50:40.940
even on this current Essential Games list, I can't...

00:50:40.940 --> 00:50:42.400
There's a lot of things that I have voted on there.

00:50:42.480 --> 00:50:45.080
I know that people won't be named.

00:50:45.080 --> 00:50:46.480
We're gunning for Spy vs.

00:50:46.660 --> 00:50:48.360
Spy last time we were trying to take things off.

00:50:48.500 --> 00:50:52.180
Like I feel like a lot of stuff on there right now,

00:50:52.180 --> 00:50:55.920
I have a hard time seeing myself at least going like,

00:50:56.360 --> 00:50:58.640
okay, yeah, that should come off now because I've seen better games.

00:50:58.740 --> 00:51:01.240
Like I think I've gotten to a point where I'm like,

00:51:01.280 --> 00:51:05.360
okay, this is where I'm thinking of these games as a whole outside of the NES.

00:51:05.580 --> 00:51:07.980
But who knows how I'll feel in another year

00:51:07.980 --> 00:51:10.300
when we're talking about the best of and I look back

00:51:10.300 --> 00:51:12.700
and I think, wait a minute, why was that on the Essential Games list?

00:51:12.700 --> 00:51:16.140
And it's interesting you bring up the every 10 episodes thing, Joe,

00:51:16.280 --> 00:51:19.240
because At Late to Gaming also brought up that

00:51:19.240 --> 00:51:21.560
if we go by just North American releases,

00:51:21.820 --> 00:51:23.440
something that this podcast is, right,

00:51:23.500 --> 00:51:27.580
a chronological exploration of every NES game released in North America,

00:51:27.820 --> 00:51:32.960
then it would only take 68 North American games

00:51:32.960 --> 00:51:35.700
to be on the Essential Games list to be essential.

00:51:35.700 --> 00:51:39.240
And the fact that we're at 22 a quarter of the way through,

00:51:40.440 --> 00:51:42.900
you know, it could come down to the wire.

00:51:43.120 --> 00:51:45.980
But, you know, like you said, there also is a chance that like

00:51:45.980 --> 00:51:50.300
not all of these 22 games last all the way to, you know,

00:51:50.460 --> 00:51:52.340
our final best of 1994 episode.

00:51:53.100 --> 00:51:54.680
Right, in 2032.

00:51:55.540 --> 00:52:02.920
Right, right. I think it's funny to, you know, to just throw out a number there real fast, guys.

